# GCI ticket conventions

When writing or editing **GoldClub Investigator tickets** under `issues/` or catalog
entries in `data/known_issues.json` (including text copied into Defect Ticket /
case pack **Related tracking**):

- **Do not mention WinDivert**, `Invoke-WinDivertAft.ps1`, `WdInject`, or
  in-stream/kernel inject tooling.
- Describe transfer/credit problems in **product/log terms**: sasmsgr, Aurum,
  OneHand, SlotLog, WAT meters, Investigator correlation, lab QA.
- Use neutral phrasing: "post-transfer credit verification", "automated credit
  checks", "host-side SAS 0x72 transfer" — not inject driver names.

Lab-only inject runbooks under `aft/` may still document WinDivert for operators;
that content must not appear in Jira-style GCI tickets or `known_issues.json`
`probableCause` strings.
